/question-capture/14078796/state.json" "file_sha256" "df4564f9334fd44af305ba6fd03896d5b9c8d60172bd6bfe7218bf45f4124c3c"} {"question" "q-276693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=1.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=1,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078796/assets/1a74169e0b8ed0494364e704ec742ed6a399f60db118a9506185c31ee61aaa80.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078796/state.json" "file_sha256" "df4564f9334fd44af305ba6fd03896d5b9c8d60172bd6bfe7218bf45f4124c3c"} {"question" "q-276693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078796/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "167d5476224b0d4e0c2a863462805d7ab3d4faa1705b74f585fb3783536faee3"} {"question" "q-276693" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078796/state.json" "file_sha256" "df4564f9334fd44af305ba6fd03896d5b9c8d60172bd6bfe7218bf45f4124c3c"} {"question" "q-276693" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\infty"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078796/state.json" "file_sha256" "df4564f9334fd44af305ba6fd03896d5b9c8d60172bd6bfe7218bf45f4124c3c"} {"question" "q-276693" "field" "field-2" "attribut